# Git is only half of what keeps the published folder clean, and the smaller half.
#
# Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
# directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published folder
# is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there, and everything else in
# this repository - Source/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by construction.

# Build intermediates. Source/Directory.Build.props redirects them to .build/ at the repository
# root, so they never land inside Mod/ and never ship; these rules catch a build run without it.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of this
# repository, and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Showcase notes: French working notes, deleted once Preview.png and ModIcon.png are done.
PROMPT_*.md

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# Texture caches. The game writes a .dds beside every PNG it loads for a mod it can write to: four
# appeared next to this mod's textures on 2026-09-23, two hours before the 0.1.0 upload. They are
# regenerated on demand, they are not the mod's content, and a checkout must not carry them.
*.dds

# Windows folder icons. The root and Mod/ carry a desktop.ini pointing at Art/ModIcon.ico and
# Art/Preview.ico. Steam sends Mod/ untouched, so neither may be tracked or reach a checkout of it.
desktop.ini
*.ico

# Test evidence stays on disk and out of git: captures and Player.log grow without a limit. What is
# kept in git is one line per run in docs/runs/, and STATUS.md points at that, never at these folders.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/

# System.
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
